title: Political Rally
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: rally_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; rally_timer = 6 if next_election_time - time > 6 and not (year == 1928 and month == 1); rally_timer = 2 if (year == 1928 and month == 1) or (next_election_time - time <= 6)
card-image: img/protest.jpg
go-to: main_rally; pfjp_collab if lwusp_votes < pfjp_votes and year <= 1955

@pfjp_collab

We aren't the only political force upholding <span style="color: #03c2fc;">refor</span><span style="color: #2b2673;">mism</span>. Should we work together with the <span style="color: #03c2fc;">**PFJP**</span>?

- @work_w_pfjp
- @dont_work

@work_w_pfjp
title: Work together with the <span style="color: #03c2fc;">**PFJP**</span>.
on-arrival: new_middle_pfjp += 1; old_middle_pfjp += 1; workers_pfjp += 1; unemployed_pfjp += 1; popular_mobilization += 1;
go-to: main_rally

We have decided to collaborate. This will likely give them more merit than they deserve, but it will also greatly increase the rally's effectiveness.

@dont_work
title: Organize the rally alone.
go-to: main_rally

We have decided to not work with the <span style="color: #03c2fc;">**PFJP**</span>.

@main_rally

Mass rallies are a common feature of <span style="color: #2b2673;">reformist</span> life, especially in the lead-up to an election. What is the primary theme of this rally?

- @reform: The reform of the current political system towards a more democratic Sordland.
- @democracy: The defense of democracy from <span style="color: #7e0b80;">Sollists</span> and <span style="color: #000000;">Nationalists</span>.
- @welfare: The expansion of the welfare state to solve economic inequality.
- @women: The emancipation of women from the patriarchy!
- @minorities: The establishment of minority rights.
- @local: A mixture of various local and national concerns that resonate most with the audience.
- @easy_discard

@reform
on-arrival: pro_republic += 4; socialism += 1; nationalism -= 1; nfp_relation -= 3; rwusp_relation -= 3; popular_mobilization  += 1; new_middle_lwusp += 2*(1 - dissent); workers_lwusp += 2*(1 - dissent); old_middle_lwusp += 2*(1 - dissent); unemployed_lwusp += 2*(1 - dissent)
view-if: reformist_constitution = 0

Our speakers fight for a more democratic system. This is broadly popular among most segments of society.

@democracy
on-arrival: democratization += 1; pro_republic += 3*(1 - dissent); new_middle_lwusp += 2; old_middle_lwusp += 1; workers_lwusp += 2*(1-dissent) if democratization >= 3; unemployed_lwusp += 1*(1-dissent) if democratization >= 3; new_middle_lwusp += 2*(1-dissent) if democratization >= 3; popular_mobilization += 1; rwusp_relation -= 3
view-if: reformist_constitution = 1

Our speakers defend the new republican system and rally against the <span style="color: #7e0b80;">Sollists</span> and <span style="color: #000000;">Nationalists</span> who threaten it.

@welfare
on-arrival: workers_lwusp += 3*(1-dissent); workers_lwusp += 3*(1-dissent) if welfare > 0; unemployed_lwusp += 3*(1-dissent) if welfare > 0; unemployed_lwusp += 4*(1-dissent) if welfare > 1; left_strength += 5; left_dissent -= 3; socialism += 1;

The message appeals to the organized workers and <span style="color: #c00000;">social democrats</span>. [? if welfare > 1 : Our achievements in expanding welfare have made this message more effective. ?]

@women
on-arrival: womens_rights += 1; pfjp_relation += 3; new_middle_lwusp += 2*(1-dissent); old_middle_lwusp += 2*(1-dissent); workers_lwusp += 2*(1-dissent); new_middle_lwusp += 2*(1-dissent) if womens_rights > 1; old_middle_lwusp += 2*(1-dissent) if womens_rights > 1; workers_lwusp += 2*(1-dissent) if womens_rights > 1; popular_mobilization += 1

The message appeals to many women in the growing feminist movement. [? if womens_rights > 1 : Our commitment to women's rights have made this message more effective. ?]


@minorities:
on-arrival: wpb_relation += 5; bluds_lwusp += 5*(1-dissent); rural_lwusp -= 2; nfp_relation -= 5; rwusp_relation -= 5

The message appeals mostly to Bludish people. Our campaign choice is regarded as being mostly ineffective.

@local
on-arrival: workers_spd += 3*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 1*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 3*(1-dissent);

Our speakers have gauged the mood and are speaking to the issues that seem to most affect the workers in this moment.
